<h2 id="qigong-one-to-one" class="reveal">Online Qigong Courses - One to One</h2>
<p style="margin-bottom:1.2em;" class="reveal"><a href="/why-qigong-training/" style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:0.82em;letter-spacing:1.5px;text-transform:uppercase;">→ Why choose this training?</a></p>

<div class="shared-story reveal">
<p>Structured courses in specific Qigong forms and practices, taught live and one to one by me, and shaped around your body, level and goals. Each course runs twice weekly, with proper time to practise between sessions - the practice, not the information, is what brings results.</p>
</div>

<h3 class="reveal">Every Course Includes</h3>
<ul class="features reveal">
<li>Live one-to-one sessions of 60 to 90 minutes, over Zoom, Microsoft Teams or Google Meet</li>
<li>Eight sessions within four weeks - the advanced Eight Extraordinary Meridians course runs ten sessions within five</li>
<li>Your course starts when you do - times arranged flexibly around your schedule and time zone</li>
<li>Full notes and diagrams for every form</li>
<li>Support between sessions, and for two months after your course ends</li>
<li>Ongoing assessment: you demonstrate, faults are corrected in real time</li>
<li>All teaching is live, with full-length posture checks - this is one-to-one tuition, not a video course</li>
</ul>

<p class="reveal">&euro;520 for an eight-session course - that's &euro;65 per session, everything included. The advanced ten-session Eight Extraordinary Meridians course is &euro;750.</p>

<h3 class="reveal">The Courses</h3>

<div class="reveal" style="border:1px solid rgba(46,90,107,0.12);border-radius:16px;padding:1.6em 1.8em;margin-bottom:1.2em;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.6);">
  <h4 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-size:1.25em;color:#2E5A6B;margin:0 0 0.4em;">Jǐnxiù Gōng</h4>
  <p style="margin:0 0 0.8em;">Seven exercises, simple to learn and remarkably deep - working the twelve meridians, opening Ming Men, clearing Dazhui and Jianjing, and training the paired skills of sinking the Qi and raising the Shen. All levels.</p>
  <p style="margin:0;"><a href="/online-courses/xiu-jin/" style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:0.82em;letter-spacing:1.5px;text-transform:uppercase;">→ Course details</a></p>
</div>

<div class="reveal" style="border:1px solid rgba(46,90,107,0.12);border-radius:16px;padding:1.6em 1.8em;margin-bottom:1.2em;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.6);">
  <h4 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-size:1.25em;color:#2E5A6B;margin:0 0 0.4em;">Heaven and Earth Qigong</h4>
  <p style="margin:0 0 0.8em;">Six movements, one complete balanced practice - taught in its Five Elements version, bringing balance across the whole meridian system while calming the mind and energising the body. All levels.</p>
  <p style="margin:0;"><a href="/online-courses/heaven-and-earth/" style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:0.82em;letter-spacing:1.5px;text-transform:uppercase;">→ Course details</a></p>
</div>

<div class="reveal" style="border:1px solid rgba(46,90,107,0.12);border-radius:16px;padding:1.6em 1.8em;margin-bottom:1.2em;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.6);">
  <h4 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-size:1.25em;color:#2E5A6B;margin:0 0 0.4em;">Bāguà Chūn Gēn</h4>
  <p style="margin:0 0 0.8em;">Eight exercises rooted in the trigrams of Taoist cosmology - opening rarely taught energy gates and working acupoints across all the meridians. Not Bāguàzhǎng: no circle walking. All levels.</p>
  <p style="margin:0;"><a href="/online-courses/bagua-chun-gen/" style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:0.82em;letter-spacing:1.5px;text-transform:uppercase;">→ Course details</a></p>
</div>

<div class="reveal" style="border:1px solid rgba(46,90,107,0.12);border-radius:16px;padding:1.6em 1.8em;margin-bottom:1.2em;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.6);">
  <h4 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-size:1.25em;color:#2E5A6B;margin:0 0 0.4em;">Eight Extraordinary Meridians Qigong</h4>
  <p style="margin:0 0 0.8em;">Working directly with the deep reservoirs of the Qi system through the Master and Coupled points. Ten sessions within five weeks. Advanced - prerequisites apply.</p>
  <p style="margin:0;"><a href="/online-courses/eight-extraordinary-meridians/" style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:0.82em;letter-spacing:1.5px;text-transform:uppercase;">→ Course details</a></p>
</div>

<div class="reveal" style="border:1px solid rgba(46,90,107,0.12);border-radius:16px;padding:1.6em 1.8em;margin-bottom:1.2em;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.6);">
  <h4 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-size:1.25em;color:#2E5A6B;margin:0 0 0.4em;">Yáng Zhànzhuāng</h4>
  <p style="margin:0 0 0.8em;">The quiet foundation beneath every internal art. A special Yang form built from a series of standing postures - structure, root, deep relaxation and tangible awareness of Qi. All levels; the ideal starting point.</p>
  <p style="margin:0;"><a href="/online-courses/zhan-zhuang/" style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:0.82em;letter-spacing:1.5px;text-transform:uppercase;">→ Course details</a></p>
</div>

<p class="reveal">Several of these forms are also taught within the <a href="#200h-qigong-teacher-training">200-Hour Qigong Teacher Training</a>, alongside additional forms, Traditional Chinese Medicine theory and teaching methodology.</p>

